# expected.subscriber.log
# attestation: spec-derived from IEEE 1516.1-2010 references below
# Cross-check status: not yet cross-checked (2-federate scenario; reproducible via the external commercial-RTI harness against any DLC-conformant RTI)
# canonicalization: cppsdk/tests/dlc/conformance/_harness/normalize.py
# spec-cites: see README.md
# Per IEEE 1516.1-2010 §4.2, §4.9, §8.5, §8.6, §5.8, §8.22, §8.13, §4.10:
SUB: CONNECT
SUB: JOIN
SUB: TIME_CONSTRAINED_ENABLED
SUB: SUBSCRIBE Honk
SUB: REQUEST_RETRACTION handle=<H>
SUB: TIME_ADVANCE_GRANT
SUB: RESIGN
# CRITICAL: per §8.21 retract() the subscriber MUST see REQUEST_RETRACTION
# BEFORE (and NEVER instead) any RECEIVE for the retracted TSO message.
# If RECEIVE_SPURIOUS appears, the retraction failed to suppress the
# original — golden diff fails.
